| OriginalAirDate = {{Start date|1996|10|5}}
| ShortSummary    = While taking driving lessons with Wolverine, Jubilee is surprised by Longshot, who is being pursued by a band of warriors led by Spiral. Wolverine assists them in driving off Spiral's party. Questioned by the X-Men, Longshot slowly regains his memories and recalls how he betrayed Mojo and took leadership of a rebellion against his dictatorship; an attempt by Mojo to then brainwash Longshot to serve him again failed when his allies stopped the procedure and sent Longshot to the X-Men's dimension to save him. Mojo arrives on Earth in person with Spiral and his crew, deciding to conquer it and setting up a televised "[[reality show|hunt]]" to once again exploit the X-Men for high ratings. Splitting up, the X-Men save Jubilee from Mojo's clutches, wreck the broadcast, and threaten him personally; having had enough, the crew hastily returns to their own dimension. Longshot is heartened by the X-Men's conviction and chooses to go back as well, vowing to see his rebellion through to completion.
