| OriginalAirDate = {{Start date|1995|2|4}}
| ShortSummary    = [[Iceman (Marvel Comics)|Iceman]], one of the five original X-Men, is forcibly subdued by his old team for breaking into a government installation. Questioned by Jubilee, Xavier explains that Iceman's defiant personality made it impossible for him to take orders, and he eventually chose to give up heroism, settling down with his girlfriend [[Polaris (Marvel Comics)|Lorna Dane]] until she disappeared. Iceman explains that he's been tracking any known clues as to her whereabouts. A moved Jubilee frees Iceman and joins him in returning to the installation. When the X-Men follow, they are confronted by a government-sponsored mutant team called [[X-Factor (comics)|X-Factor]]. To Iceman's shock, not only is Lorna a member, but is also in a relationship with her teammate [[Havok (character)|Havok]]. Team leader [[Forge (character)|Forge]] backs up Lorna when she chooses to stay with X-Factor; Iceman decides to resume his civilian identity as Bobby Drake, telling Xavier that he's content.
